error[E0303]: a condition literal does not support a key that is not a field name
  --> where_literal_unsupported.bit:14:29
   |
14 |   let a: Where<Article> = { "score": 1 }
   |                             ^^^^^^^ write `field: value`, `field: { gte: value }`, `field: related("name")`, or an `and`/`or`/`not` key
error[E0303]: a condition literal does not support an operator object with no operator
  --> where_literal_unsupported.bit:15:36
   |
15 |   let b: Where<Article> = { score: {} }
   |                                    ^^ write `field: value`, `field: { gte: value }`, `field: related("name")`, or an `and`/`or`/`not` key
error[E0303]: a condition literal does not support an operator that is not a plain name
  --> where_literal_unsupported.bit:16:38
   |
16 |   let c: Where<Article> = { score: { "gte": 1 } }
   |                                      ^^^^^ write `field: value`, `field: { gte: value }`, `field: related("name")`, or an `and`/`or`/`not` key
